  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Policy Research into the Role of Faith Leaders in the Ebola Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Faith leaders and faith based organisations have played a key role in addressing the ebola disease outbreak in Sierra Leone. Faith has a huge place in people&#x2019;s lives in countries like Sierra Leone, Liberia and Guinea where the majority of the population are practicing believers. They listen to their faith leaders and often come to places of worship for reliable information.  The messages of the faith leaders can resonate with their congregations and when the NGOs are no longer around or unable to reach really remote communities the faith leaders and their sensitisation work will remain. 

This research, which is commissioned by an inter-agency, inter-faith group comprising CAFOD, Islamic Relief, Christian Aid and Tearfund, will provide an evidence base on the role of faith leaders in addressing the Ebola outbreak particularly in relation to prevention, social mobilisation and stigmatisation.</narrative>
  </description>
